diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/drop-debian-erlang-ppa-f0e5625a060f55a9.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/drop-debian-erlang-ppa-f0e5625a060f55a9.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e6fdf3364
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/drop-debian-erlang-ppa-f0e5625a060f55a9.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    The ``kolla-toolbox`` and ``rabbitmq`` images on Debian no longer
+    enable the ``rabbitmq-erlang`` PPA hosted on Launchpad
+    (``ppa.launchpadcontent.net``). Debian Trixie now ships
+    ``erlang-base`` 1:27.x in its base archive, which already satisfies
+    the ``erlang* version 1:27.*`` pin in
+    ``apt_preferences_rabbitmq.debian``. The ``rabbitmq-server`` package
+    continues to come from ``deb1.rabbitmq.com``.
+
+    Similarly,  the Ubuntu ``amd64`` image builds use the RabbitMQ team's
+    own Debian/Ubuntu mirror. However, the RabbitMQ-hosted packages are
+    Only build for ``amd64``, so ``ubuntu-aarch64`` builds continue to
+    enable the Launchpad PPA via an ``ubuntu-aarch64`` override in
+    ``kolla/template/repos.yaml``. Until the RabbitMQ team publishes
+    ``arm64`` builds, ``arm64`` Ubuntu image builds remain dependent
+    on Launchpad availability for Erlang.
